{
  "info": {
    "name": "SOTWISE — GSS Orders (POST + GET)",
    "description": "Teste da via inbound GSS → SOTWISE que agenda (schedule) orders.\n\nEndpoints: POST /api/gss/orders (o GSS cria/atualiza) e GET /api/gss/orders (o GSS lê status, lote e checklist)\nAuth: Authorization: Bearer {{gss_inbound_secret}} (server-to-server, NÃO é o API_TOKEN dos cadastros)\n\nO campo central do agendamento é `schedule_requested` (data YYYY-MM-DD). O POST é idempotente por `gss_id`: reenviar o mesmo gss_id ATUALIZA a order (não duplica). `po_number` é unique no banco — colisão devolve 409. O checklist das 10 etapas é semeado pelo trigger `trg_orders_seed_checklist` a cada INSERT.\n\nRode a collection inteira em ordem (Runner): as requisições geram um gss_id/po_number únicos por execução, então não colidem entre rodadas.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{gss_inbound_secret}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Gera um gss_id/po_number únicos por execução da collection,",
          "// para que rodadas repetidas não colidam (409) sem querer.",
          "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('run_stamp')) {",
          "  const stamp = Date.now().toString();",
          "  pm.collectionVariables.set('run_stamp', stamp);",
          "  pm.collectionVariables.set('run_gss_id', 'GSS-TEST-' + stamp);",
          "  pm.collectionVariables.set('run_po_number', 'PO-TEST-' + stamp);",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "https://sotwise-pi.vercel.app",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "run_stamp",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "run_gss_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "run_po_number",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "created_order_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Agendar order (criar) — 201",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/gss/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "gss",
            "orders"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"gss_id\": \"{{run_gss_id}}\",\n  \"po_number\": \"{{run_po_number}}\",\n  \"schedule_requested\": \"2026-09-15\",\n  \"client_reference\": \"REF via Postman\",\n  \"date_po\": \"2026-08-25\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "Cria uma order agendada. Só `gss_id` e `po_number` são obrigatórios; `schedule_requested` é a data do agendamento. As FKs de biblioteca (order_type_gss_id, client_gss_id, business_unit_gss_id, exporter_gss_id) são opcionais e resolvidas pelo gss_id da lib — ver a requisição 7."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 201 (criada)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('created === true', () => pm.expect(b.created).to.eql(true));",
              "pm.test('devolve id e po_number', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(b.data).to.have.property('id');",
              "  pm.expect(b.data.po_number).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('run_po_number'));",
              "});",
              "if (b.data && b.data.id) pm.collectionVariables.set('created_order_id', b.data.id);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Reenviar mesma order (idempotente / atualiza) — 200",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/gss/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "gss",
            "orders"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"gss_id\": \"{{run_gss_id}}\",\n  \"po_number\": \"{{run_po_number}}\",\n  \"schedule_requested\": \"2026-10-01\",\n  \"client_reference\": \"REF atualizada via Postman\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "Mesmo `gss_id` da requisição 1: o endpoint faz UPDATE em vez de INSERT (idempotência). Note o `schedule_requested` mudado — deve refletir na order sem criar duplicata."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 200 (atualizada)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('created === false', () => pm.expect(b.created).to.eql(false));",
              "pm.test('mesmo id da criação (não duplicou)', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(b.data.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('created_order_id'));",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Colisão de po_number — 409",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/gss/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "gss",
            "orders"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"gss_id\": \"{{run_gss_id}}-B\",\n  \"po_number\": \"{{run_po_number}}\",\n  \"schedule_requested\": \"2026-09-20\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "gss_id NOVO mas o MESMO po_number da requisição 1. `po_number` é unique no banco → 409."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 409 (po_number em uso)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
              "pm.test('mensagem menciona po_number', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.toLowerCase()).to.include('po_number');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Sem autenticação — 401",
      "request": {
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/gss/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "gss",
            "orders"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"gss_id\": \"{{run_gss_id}}-NOAUTH\",\n  \"po_number\": \"{{run_po_number}}-NOAUTH\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "Sem o header Authorization (auth = No Auth). Deve responder 401 antes de tocar no banco."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Payload inválido (sem po_number) — 400",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/gss/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "gss",
            "orders"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"gss_id\": \"{{run_gss_id}}-INVALID\",\n  \"schedule_requested\": \"2026-09-15\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "Falta o `po_number` (obrigatório). O schema Zod rejeita → 400 com `error` + lista `issues`."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
              "pm.test('erro menciona po_number (obrigatório na criação)', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.toLowerCase()).to.include('po_number');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. schedule_requested com formato errado — 400",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/gss/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "gss",
            "orders"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"gss_id\": \"{{run_gss_id}}-BADDATE\",\n  \"po_number\": \"{{run_po_number}}-BADDATE\",\n  \"schedule_requested\": \"15/09/2026\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "`schedule_requested` precisa ser YYYY-MM-DD. Data em outro formato → 400 (\"Date must be YYYY-MM-DD.\")."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
              "pm.test('mensagem cita o formato de data', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.include('YYYY-MM-DD');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "7. FK de biblioteca inexistente — 400",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/gss/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "gss",
            "orders"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"gss_id\": \"{{run_gss_id}}-FK\",\n  \"po_number\": \"{{run_po_number}}-FK\",\n  \"schedule_requested\": \"2026-09-15\",\n  \"client_gss_id\": \"NAO-EXISTE-NO-GSS\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "Um `*_gss_id` de biblioteca que não existe no SOTWISE não resolve para UUID → 400 (\"No clients found for gss_id '…'.\")."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
              "pm.test('mensagem cita o gss_id não resolvido', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.toLowerCase()).to.include('gss_id');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "8. Agendar com FKs de biblioteca (template) — 201",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/gss/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "gss",
            "orders"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          },
          "raw": "{\n  \"gss_id\": \"{{run_gss_id}}-FULL\",\n  \"po_number\": \"{{run_po_number}}-FULL\",\n  \"schedule_requested\": \"2026-09-15\",\n  \"client_reference\": \"Pedido completo\",\n  \"date_po\": \"2026-08-25\",\n  \"order_type_gss_id\": \"{{order_type_gss_id}}\",\n  \"client_gss_id\": \"{{client_gss_id}}\",\n  \"business_unit_gss_id\": \"{{business_unit_gss_id}}\",\n  \"exporter_gss_id\": \"{{exporter_gss_id}}\",\n  \"leader_email\": \"{{leader_email}}\",\n  \"requester_email\": \"{{requester_email}}\",\n  \"items\": [\n    { \"supplier_category_gss_id\": \"{{supplier_category_gss_id_1}}\", \"ship_requirement\": \"2026-09-10\" },\n    { \"supplier_category_gss_id\": \"{{supplier_category_gss_id_2}}\", \"ship_requirement\": \"2026-09-15\" }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        "description": "Exemplo COMPLETO com as 4 FKs de biblioteca resolvidas por gss_id. Preencha as variáveis order_type_gss_id / client_gss_id / business_unit_gss_id / exporter_gss_id no environment com valores REAIS do GSS antes de rodar — senão cai no 400 da requisição 7. Por isso fica fora do fluxo padrão (desabilite ou pule no Runner se não tiver os gss_ids)."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Só valida quando as 4 FKs foram preenchidas no environment.",
              "const filled = ['order_type_gss_id','client_gss_id','business_unit_gss_id','exporter_gss_id']",
              "  .every(k => (pm.variables.get(k) || '').length > 0);",
              "if (!filled) {",
              "  pm.test.skip('FKs de biblioteca não preenchidas — pulando (ver descrição)');",
              "} else {",
              "  pm.test('status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "9. Listar orders (página) — 200",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/gss/orders?limit=5&order=desc",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "gss",
            "orders"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "limit",
              "value": "5",
              "description": "1–200 (default 50)"
            },
            {
              "key": "order",
              "value": "desc",
              "description": "asc | desc, por updated_at (default desc)"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Lista as orders mais recentes. A resposta é SEMPRE uma lista, com `pagination` (limit/offset/returned/total). As bibliotecas vêm como { id, name, gss_id } — o gss_id é a chave que o GSS usa para reconciliar."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('devolve data[] e pagination', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(b.data).to.be.an('array');",
              "  pm.expect(b.pagination).to.have.property('total');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('respeita o limit', () => pm.expect(b.data.length).to.be.at.most(5));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "10. Ler a order criada (gss_id + include) — 200",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/gss/orders?gss_id={{run_gss_id}}&include=items,checklist",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "gss",
            "orders"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "gss_id",
              "value": "{{run_gss_id}}",
              "description": "id do pedido no GSS (o mesmo do POST)"
            },
            {
              "key": "include",
              "value": "items,checklist",
              "description": "blocos extras: items | checklist"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Lê de volta a order criada na requisição 1, com as linhas Factory×Category (incluindo o lote atribuído no SOTWISE) e as 10 etapas do checklist da fase Order. Filtrar por gss_id NÃO muda a forma da resposta: continua uma lista, de 0 ou 1 item."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('achou exatamente a order do POST', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(b.data.length).to.eql(1);",
              "  pm.expect(b.data[0].gss_id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('run_gss_id'));",
              "});",
              "pm.test('include trouxe items e checklist', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(b.data[0].items).to.be.an('array');",
              "  pm.expect(b.data[0].checklist).to.be.an('array');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('o trigger semeou as 10 etapas da fase Order', () =>",
              "  pm.expect(b.data[0].checklist.length).to.eql(10));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "11. Sincronização incremental (updated_since) — 200",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/gss/orders?updated_since=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&order=asc&limit=50",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "gss",
            "orders"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "updated_since",
              "value": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
              "description": "ISO 8601 com fuso — só o que mudou desde então"
            },
            {
              "key": "order",
              "value": "asc",
              "description": "cronológico, para varrer sem pular nada"
            },
            {
              "key": "limit",
              "value": "50",
              "description": "pagine com offset até returned < limit"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "O uso principal do GET pelo GSS: guardar o maior updated_at já visto e pedir só o que mudou desde então. A ordenação é updated_at + id (o id desempata, então nenhuma order pula nem repete entre páginas)."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('vem em ordem cronológica', () => {",
              "  const dates = b.data.map((o) => o.updated_at);",
              "  pm.expect(dates).to.eql([...dates].sort());",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "12. Query param inválido — 400",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/gss/orders?status=nao_existe",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "gss",
            "orders"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "status",
              "value": "nao_existe",
              "description": "status fora da lista de OrderStatus"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Valor inválido em query param responde 400 com `issues[]` apontando o campo — mesmo padrão de erro do POST."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
              "pm.test('aponta o campo com problema', () => {",
              "  const b = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(b.error).to.include('status');",
              "  pm.expect(b.issues).to.be.an('array');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
